## Checks of the Review A row (test-strategy line 368)

- The merge result is clean. The login signed-media map (lib/media/sign.ts,
  lib/media/url.ts) gives every look view its URLs: signWeekMedia signs every path that
  mediaPathsOf walks outside approval.*, and the walk finds the new wordClips paths.
- The thin-component rule holds: highestOpenWeeks lives in lib/content.ts and replicates
  the loadVisibleWeek rule with no log; parseStorytimePath lives in lib/route-parse.ts;
  the client 404 child only reads the path and renders.
- The 404 client/server split is correct: not-found.tsx is a server component with no
  props; not-found-view.tsx is a client component that imports neither node:fs nor
  lib/content and reads messages/en.json (default Q-C). The link is built from the locale
  prop and two integers, never from the path text.
- The packages/read-along change is additive (wordIsTarget) plus the pseudo-element hit
  area; the package hook use-read-along.ts is unmodified and the reader reuses its one
  frame loop.
- The old-test edits hold R-EDIT. The mock edits (lib/media/url, lib/media/sign,
  lib/auth) add setup only. The decodable-punct, loops-off, and audio-seek-stop edits are
  each needed and none weakens an assertion.
- The reader holds no wordCutBounds, cutEnd, seekAndRun, or stopAtMediaEnd; no dead ref
  stays. The clip lookup uses Object.hasOwn with the lower-case audio word.
- The wordClips and videoLeadInSeconds schema rules match the pins (Q10, Q18): key
  allowlist with the inherited-property refusal, mediaPath values, defaults {} and 0.
- mediaOf lists each clip once with kind word-clip; the at-home receiver tests stayed
  green (the guard run of Green round 2 passed 102 of 102, and my 535-test run includes
  them).
- onTimeUpdate keeps the stop logic and still moves the highlight (default Q-G), so the
  old timeupdate tests stay green.
- preload is "metadata" on the song video; the stage holds the poster as an inline
  background until the playing event, and the video background is transparent until a
  frame plays, so the black .song-stage video rule cannot hide the poster (Q13 note).
- Red-before-Green holds for every look file. The r4 fix 7b896cf8d resolves D1 to D6.
  Commit 6bd0ed1fe records old_cases_removed=8.

## Green defaults

- Q-A: Next is disabled on the last page only when the reader has no tiles and no
  questions (hasEnd). The shipped page always passes tiles.
- Q-B: only a press on Next holds the page; Previous and a swipe turn at once.
- Q-C: the client 404 view imports messages/en.json.
- Q-D: the hit area is a pseudo-element 0.25 rem wider on each side and 0.5 rem higher
  above and below. See finding N2.
- Q-E: app/icon.png comes from q-crest.svg (10215 bytes, named in the commit body).
- Q-F: ReaderLabels.playing is optional with a locale default (DEFAULT_PLAYING).
- Q-G: timeupdate still moves the highlight; the frame loop is the main driver.

